phi-transport-api (2.0.0-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Version the package by the API version instead of a git snapshot. The
    interface version is what consumers depend on (see the load-time version gate),
    so it has to be expressible as a package relation - phi-transport-api-dev
    (>= 2.0.0) was unsatisfiable while the package called itself 0.0~git...
    Matches the convention of phi-adapter-sdk.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 22:21:08 +0200

phi-transport-api (0.0~git202608192218.3710e87-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Interface break: TransportInterface is stateless and the core facade plus the
    log/call helpers moved to the new header-only TransportPluginBase. Transports
    derive from the base and drop their apiVersion() override.
  * Plugin IID bumped to .../TransportInterface/2.0 and kTransportApiVersion
    added: phi-core refuses a transport built against another interface version at
    load instead of binding it to a mismatched vtable (F-38).
  * Documented that this is a public source API with no binary compatibility, and
    that adapters (southbound) and transports (northbound) are told apart by
    direction rather than by protocol name.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 22:18:53 +0200

phi-transport-api (0.0~git202608192046.3b2b174-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Document what CoreFacade::invokeSync's timeout bounds - the handoff to core's
    thread, not the work - and that it must be greater than zero (F-37).

